# Always check out shell scripts with LF line endings, regardless of host OS.
# Prevents Windows CRLF from sneaking into files that will run on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Apply the same rule to other files that will be consumed by Linux tools.
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Markdown can go either way; let git auto-handle based on content.
*.md text